course: dictionary
lesson: 10595
title: Understand: knowing what something means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To understand something is to know what it means or how it works. You can also understand a person, which means you know how they feel or why they act as they do. Teachers often ask «Do you understand?», and it is fine to say no and ask again.
explain: Understand has four forms you will see: understand, understands, understood and understanding. Understanding can also describe someone who is kind and forgiving. «I understand that …» can mean «I have heard that …», so read the words around it to check which meaning fits.
explain: Look at this: «Playing a game with a parent who talks about it can make it less frightening and easier to understand.» The clue is in the words around understand: less frightening and easier. Ask yourself: what would make the game easier to follow? Knowing what it is about.
fact: To understand means to know what something means or how it works.
fact: «Understood» is the past form: «Koko the gorilla used many signs, but scientists still argue how much she understood.»
fact: Understanding can also mean kind and forgiving, as in «understanding» teachers who let you try again.
fact: To make yourself understood means to say something clearly enough for other people to get your meaning.
fact: In school, you understand a maths method when you can explain why it works, not just remember the steps.
exercise: «Owning up and asking for help with the part you didn't understand is the real fix for cheating in learning.» What does didn't understand mean here? | Did not like the lesson | Did not finish the work on time | *Did not know what it meant or how it worked | Did not hear the teacher at all
exercise: «Memes and comedy can spark curiosity, but you need to know the real story to understand the joke.» What does understand mean here? | Forget the joke quickly | Laugh very loudly | Tell the joke to others | *Know what the joke means
exercise: A friend says, «I understand that the trip is cancelled.» Which meaning fits best? | I feel sorry for the people going | I know how the trip works | *I have heard that the trip is cancelled | I have decided to go anyway
test: Which word is the past form of understand? | Understands | *Understood | Understanding
test: Sami says his teacher is very understanding when he is late. What does understanding mean here? | Able to explain a method | Very loud | *Kind and forgiving | Angry and strict
exam: In «Do you understand?», what is the teacher asking? | Whether you have finished your homework | Whether you are tall enough for the ride | Whether you want more lunch | *Whether you know what something means
